  "final_text": "Both objects exist. The dashboard has five panels and the alert rule is enabled.\n\n**Data exploration:** The data view `kibana_sample_data_logs` has 46 fields, but I could not query the values. `KIBANA_TEST_API_KEY` is not set in my shell, so direct Kibana calls return 401. I worked from the field list. The key fields are `timestamp` (time field), `response` / `response.keyword` (status code, stored as a string), `bytes`, `url.keyword`, `geo.dest`, `machine.os.keyword`, and `clientip`. The dashboard and rule were built through the MCP tools, which have their own connection.\n\n**Dashboard: `EFF-05fb5009 Web logs overview`**\n- ID: `eff-05fb5009-web-logs-overview-dd5d8d17cf1c`\n- Total requests (metric, count)\n- Average response size in bytes (metric, average of `bytes`)\n- Requests over time (line, date histogram on `timestamp`)\n- Responses by status code (bar, terms on `response.keyword`)\n- 5xx responses (ES|QL metric, `COUNT(*)` where `TO_INTEGER(response)` is 500\u2013599)\n- Time range: last 5 years. I chose this because the sample data's timestamps may be far from today's date (2026-10-12). Narrow it if you want a shorter window.\n\n**Alert rule: `EFF-05fb5009 5xx spike`**\n- ID: `cd6168e9-1409-4ae5-b95f-e6c17ecbe856`\n- Type `.es-query`, consumer `stackAlerts`, tag `EFF-05fb5009`\n- Runs every 1m. Fires when more than 10 hits match in the last 5m.\n- Match condition: DSL filter `wildcard` on `response.keyword` with value `5*`.\n- Status: enabled. The status shows \"pending\" until the first run.\n\nI did not check that the 5xx filter matches any documents, because I couldn't run queries. The 5xx panel will show whether it does once the dashboard is opened.",
